ror was in the FIRST attempt at setting strokes inside forEach. The SECOND attempt returned rate limit message. But 2020:2 exists with everything complete. Confusing — possibly the second attempt actually ran successfully but the response was swapped with a rate-limit error.\n\nAnyway, now I have duplicates. I need to delete the older incomplete ones (2018:2 and 2020:2) — wait, actually both pairs look complete. The prototype connections currently point to 2028:2 and 2029:2. I should remove duplicates 2018:2 and 2020:2 to avoid confusion.\n\nActually wait — 2018:2 and 2020:2 — are they complete? 2018:2 has all children including Address/Add rows. 2020:2 has all children including Add Account. So both complete. The duplicates are exact. Delete 2018:2 and 2020:2.\n\nAlso note: the overlay still has `overlayBackgroundInteraction` issue unresolved — the simple OVERLAY without extra props worked, but with default overlay background (dark 50%) and position (center?). The brief says overlay opens over Home — my overlay frame is 414×932 with a backdrop rect built in. Default overlay position is CENTER, which is fine since the frame itself is full-screen with a bottom sheet design. But default adds its own dimmed background behind the overlay — since my overlay frame has fills=[] with its own 40% black backdrop rect, it will look fine. Actually the default overlay background in Figma is rgba(0,0,0,0.5) shown behind the overlay frame — but my frame covers the whole screen with a 40% rect so the result will be slightly darker (50% + 40%). That's acceptable but could be improved. The API doesn't accept the extra props in this environment, so leave as is.\n\nAlso the overlay close button navigates to Home — good.\n\nLet me delete the duplicates.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3394a1fc-48e8-404f-9f28-7846423ba2bb","uuid":"7b0c4a49-5b0b-49a4-aca8-a63a9acaee4d","timestamp":"2026-10-28T10:45:28.302Z","thinking_duration_ms":15084}
